# Hard guarantee that nothing outside the runtime input surface ever
# leaks into the image, no matter what's in the developer's worktree.
#
# The Dockerfile's COPY commands already select specific paths, so this
# is defence-in-depth + it shrinks the build context that buildx ships
# to the daemon (faster builds on tiny diffs).

# Build artefacts
target/
**/target/

# Hydrated at build time inside the builder stage; the host copy (if any)
# is irrelevant to the image and may be the wrong version.
external/

# Dev tooling and authoring tools — see CLAUDE.md "what goes in the image".
deprecated/
docs/
ghidra/
fuzz/
frontend/
bootstrap/
projects/
src/
python/
logs/
data/scripts/
data/spaces/cooked/
audit_dup_chains.py
db.bat
setup.ps1
patch-client.ps1
build.sh

# IDE + VCS
.git/
.github/
!.github/workflows/release-container.yml
!.github/workflows/prune-container.yml
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Built launcher exe at the repo root (rebuilt every PR by setup.ps1).
sgw-launcher.exe
*.dll
*.pdb

# Markdown — release notes are generated, the worktree's are docs.
*.md
!docker/**/*.md
